{
 "title": "Advanced animation 2: actions and the NLA editor",
 "summary": "Nonlinear animation: three named actions made in the Action Editor on a Suzanne (UpDown: up 3 m at frame 50 and down by 100; RotateZ: 180 degrees and back; MoveX: along X by 40 and back by 80, all full location/rotation/scale keys), pushed down into NLA tracks. The upper track replaces the lower (only the rotation plays); a track's checkbox mutes it, the star solos it; a strip dragged to another track and back; Combine blending layers them so the Suzanne moves, turns and rises at once. Beyond the tutorial: the same actions reused on a second Suzanne and rearranged (UpDown at double speed, repeated; RotateZ starting at frame 20).",
 "objects": [
  {
   "name": "MainMonkey",
   "description": "the three actions combined"
  },
  {
   "name": "EchoMonkey",
   "description": "the same actions rearranged"
  }
 ],
 "expected_result": "Two Suzannes (orange and blue) rising, turning and sliding along X over a grey floor, the blue one bouncing twice as often.",
